Phase 1. In Timeframes H4, H1, M30, And M15 Identify All The Previous Support, Resistance, Support Became Resistance (SBR), And Resistance Became Support (RBS) And Mark As Entry Lines.
   Support and resistance are key price levels where market moves pause or reverse. Support is a floor where buying stops drops. Resistance is a ceiling where selling stops rises.
   SBR means Support Becomes Resistance after a break. RBS means Resistance Becomes Support. Specific candlestick patterns build and confirm these pivotal zones.
     - Support: Price drops, hits a floor, and buyers step in.
     - Resistance: Price rises, hits a ceiling, and sellers step in.
     - Role Reversal: Broken support turns into resistance (SBR). Broken resistance turns into support (RBS).
   SBR and RBS Explained :
     - SBR (Support Becomes Resistance): Price falls below an old support line. Later, when price rises back to this line, sellers push it down.
     - RBS (Resistance Becomes Support): Price breaks above an old resistance line. Later, when price drops back to this line, buyers push it up.
   Candlesticks That Build Levels :
     - Pin Bar (Hammer / Shooting Star): Long wicks show rejection of a price. A hammer at the low creates support. A shooting star at the high creates resistance.
     - Engulfing Candle: A large body completely covers the prior candle. A bullish engulfing candle shows buyers taking over at support. A bearish engulfing candle shows sellers taking over at resistance.
     - Doji: Open and close are equal. It shows market indecision. It often forms right at turning points before a strong move.
     - Morning Star / Evening Star: Three-candle patterns. They signal strong reversals at major tops or bottoms.

