       - 2. (M5) Break of Structure (BOS). A Break of Structure is proof that a trend is healthy and moving forward. It requires the market to clear out old boundaries decisively.
                Sell Condition : Bearish BOS (Downtrend), Find the lowest point of the last downward wave (the previous Swing Low). A red candle must push below that floor and close its solid body underneath it.
                Buy Condition : Bullish BOS (Uptrend), Find the highest point of the last upward wave (the previous Swing High). A new green candle must push past that peak and close its solid body above that old high line.
                BOS Rule : If a candle only pokes its thin wick through the line but the solid body shrinks back and closes inside, it is a fake-out, not a BOS.

       - 3. (M5) Change of Character (CHoCH). CHoCH happens when a trend flips direction for the first time. It is the very first sign of a trend reversal.
               Sell Condition : Bearish CHoCH :
                   - As Price climbs into Entry Line, it was making a staircase upward (higher highs and higher lows).
                   - Spot the final, highest candle at the very top of the Entry Line.
                   - Spot just slightly to the recent candles and find the last minor "staircase peak" (the last minor low) that caused that final up.
                   - When a new red candle aggressively charges downward and closes its solid body below that last minor peak, the character of the market has changed from bullish to bearish.
               Buy Condition : Bullish CHoCH :
                   - As Price falls into Entry Line., it was making a staircase downward (lower highs and lower lows).
                   - Spot the final, lowest candle at the very bottom of the Entry Line.
                   - Spot just slightly to the recent candles and find the last minor "staircase peak" (the last minor high) that caused that final drop.
                   - When a new green candle aggressively charges upward and closes its solid body above that last minor peak, the character of the market has changed from bearish to bullish.

       - 4. (M5) Equal High(EQH) And Equal Low(EQL).
            Equal highs (EQH) and equal lows (EQL) are clusters of identical swing peaks or valleys.
                   - The Core Difference: Classic retail analysis views these as strong double tops or double bottoms. Smart money analysis treats them as magnetic fuel or liquidity pools where breakout orders and stop-losses cluster.
                   - The Liquidity Sweep: Institutional traders often push the price slightly past these equal levels to trigger those trapped orders, gathering enough volume to execute their own large trades before reversing the market direction.
               Sell Condition : Buy-Side Liquidity / Equal High (EQH): Two or more swing highs that stall or peak at a similar price level Built right Around Entry Line Area.
               Buy Codition : Sell-Side Liquidity / Equal Low (EQL): Two or more swing lows that bottom out or stall at a similar price level Built right Around Entry Line Area.

